## 7. Next steps, in order

1. ~~**Judge test–retest**~~ **Done 2026-09-18** (§3): judge instability is κ 0.87–0.96, so the
   κ ≈ 0.5 in §3c is definitional, not noise. Majority-of-3 was no more repeatable than a
   single judge.
2. **Run the rewrite test on sycophancy** (§8): draft 110 rewrites, hand-check them, run the 8
   current models under all three judges, score the CoT for template recognition on both arms.
3. **Sharpen the two ambiguous rubrics and re-judge** (optional, ~$15 each): harmful generation
   as "complied" vs "usable as-is"; sneaking as "silent substitution" vs "disclosed alternative."
   Turns one fuzzy number into two clear ones. Only if those categories stay in the paper.
4. **Round-2 hand labels for sneaking and brand-bias are deprioritised** (decision 2026-09-17):
   the definitions have the same ambiguity found in harmful generation, so more labels would
   document the fuzz rather than remove it. The blind sample stays available
   (`data/results/handlabel/sneaking_brandbias_auditing.md`) if time allows; until then both
   categories are reported as unvalidated.
5. **Annotator self-consistency**: re-label ~30 round-1 items blind after a gap, for a ceiling κ.
6. ~~**Verify every `[verify]` citation**~~ **Done 2026-09-22**: the paper's 48%/30–61% figures,
   its annotator-validation numbers, and the Claude-family-vs-single-model distinction are all
   confirmed and corrected in §1. The prior-work citations inside §8 (not yet written) remain to
   be checked once that section is drafted.
7. **Writeup**: fold §8's results into Part II and Part III once they land; final read-through.
